# Jaystarbliss Studios — Detailed Development History

Review period: approximately 22 May – 22 October 2026 | Focus: website, LMS, portals, Firebase, student accounts, examinations, dashboards, payments, GitHub and Netlify

Jaystarbliss Studios has gone through several major development phases over this period. What began as a website and multi-role learning platform has evolved into a much more interconnected system for students, parents, tutors, school administrators and platform administrators.

The most important theme running through the work is this: we have been moving the platform away from a UI that merely looks functional and toward one where real records, permissions, workflows and server-side operations determine what users can actually do. That has required adding features, correcting old assumptions, tightening security and revisiting some earlier changes when they caused compatibility problems.

I reviewed the available project history, remembered work and GitHub pull requests. One qualification: the detailed, verifiable development trail available to me is concentrated in August–October 2026, especially September and October. I can explain the work in those records with specific commits and pull requests, but I won't invent a day-by-day history for May–July where I don't have sufficient evidence.

## 1. Executive summary

Firebase and data integrity

We aligned application data with the correct Firestore database, removed fabricated dashboard information, improved account provisioning and tightened access to student, parent and school records.

LMS and academic workflows

We developed assignments, submissions, grading, feedback, attendance and progress tracking, then integrated a comprehensive examination system into the existing portal.

Authentication and permissions

We moved sensitive student access-code verification to trusted server functions, restored compatibility for older student records and corrected a database mismatch affecting login.

Billing, wallets and payouts

We removed demo financial data, worked on Firebase-backed wallet records and implemented a bank-only withdrawal workflow with Paystack bank lookup and account resolution.

UI, mobile usability and deployment

We established a reusable design system, improved responsive layouts and repeatedly repaired Netlify build failures so the application could compile and deploy reliably.

## 2. The technical foundation we were working with

The main project is the Jaystarbliss Studios website and learning platform:

- GitHub repository: [V3-JAYSTARBLISS-STUDIOS-MAIN-WEBSITE](https://github.com/jaystarbliss-dynamic-hub/V3-JAYSTARBLISS-STUDIOS-MAIN-WEBSITE?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
- Production domain: [jaystarbliss-studios.name.ng](https://jaystarbliss-studios.name.ng/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)
- Netlify project: `jaystarbliss-studios`
- Frontend: React, TypeScript and Vite.
- Backend and platform services: Firebase Authentication, Firestore, Firebase Admin SDK and Netlify Functions.
