### 4.5 Repairing repeated Netlify build failures

During this same period, the production build repeatedly failed on TypeScript errors.

The documented sequence was:

- [PR #17](https://github.com/jaystarbliss-dynamic-hub/V3-JAYSTARBLISS-STUDIOS-MAIN-WEBSITE/pull/17?utm_source=chatgpt.com) addressed a missing icon reference and cascading status-badge type errors.
- [PR #18](https://github.com/jaystarbliss-dynamic-hub/V3-JAYSTARBLISS-STUDIOS-MAIN-WEBSITE/pull/18?utm_source=chatgpt.com) then removed a brittle workaround that modified source files during the prebuild stage.
- [PR #20](https://github.com/jaystarbliss-dynamic-hub/V3-JAYSTARBLISS-STUDIOS-MAIN-WEBSITE/pull/20?utm_source=chatgpt.com) corrected missing fields in the TypeScript types for learning-track data.

The significant lesson from PR #17 and #18 was that a deployment should compile the actual committed source. A prebuild script that searches for an exact piece of source text can break when the source changes, even if the intended fix has already been applied.

The project therefore moved away from source mutation during deployment and back toward fixing the underlying code and running the normal build command.

