## Final assessment

The major development effort has been about making Jaystarbliss Studios a coherent learning platform rather than a collection of separate dashboards. The academic workflows, examination system, parent/school reporting, real-data integrity, role-based permissions and server-side authentication are all parts of that same goal.

Three lessons stand out:

1. Correct data and correct permissions matter as much as the interface. A polished dashboard is not reliable if it displays invented values or accesses the wrong records.
2. Security changes must preserve legitimate historical workflows. Moving authentication to the server was the right architectural direction, but the older student-record formats still needed deliberate compatibility support.
3. A merged PR and passing CI are not the finish line. The final proof is a successful deployed application with real, authorised accounts and complete workflows.

The most urgent unresolved question in the latest recorded history is therefore not whether another student-login patch was merged. It is whether the deployed production version now allows both existing and newly onboarded students to authenticate, and whether their schedules, examinations and other protected records load correctly after authentication. That remains unconfirmed by the evidence available here.